n-names>MD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effects of program and patient characteristics on retention of drug treatment patients</article-title><source>Evaluation and Program Planning</source><year>2001</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>331</fpage><lpage>341</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0149-7189(01)00027-1</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beynon</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Bellis</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Millar</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Meier</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomson</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Mackway-Jones</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hidden need for drug treatment services: measuring problematic drug use in the North West of England</article-title><source>Journal of Public Health Medicine</source><year>2001</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>286</fpage><lpage>291</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11873890</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>National Treatment Agency for Substance Misuse</collab></person-group><article-title>Statistics for drug treatment activity in England 2005/06 from the National Drug Treatment Monitoring System</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.nta.nhs.uk/"/></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>National Treatment Agency for Substance Misuse</collab></person-group><source>Models of Care for Substance Misuse</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>London, National Treatment Agency for Substance Misuse</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Office of the Deputy Prime Minister</collab></person-group><source>The English Indices of Deprivation 2004: Summary (revised)</source><publisher-name>London , Office of the Deputy Prime Minister</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beynon</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Bellis</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>McVeigh</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Trends in drop out, drug free discharge and rates of representation: a retrospective cohort study of drug treatment clients in the North West of England</article-title><source>BMC Public Health</source><year>2006</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>205</fpage><lpage>213</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16904004</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1471-2458-6-205</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hills</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>De Stavola</surname><given-names>BL</given-names></name></person-group><source>A short introduction to STATA 8 for biostatistics</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>London, Timberlake Consultants Ltd.</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Office of National Statistics</collab></person-group><article-title>KS06 Ethnic group</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.statistics.gov.uk/statbase/Expodata/Spreadsheets/D6561.xls"/></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>National Treatment Agency for Substance Misuse</collab></person-group><source>Black and minority ethnic communities in England: a review of the literature on drug use and related service provision</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>London, National Treatment Agency for Substance Misuse</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Patel</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Wibberley</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Young Asians and drug use</article-title><source>Journal of Child Health Care</source><year>2002</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>51</fpage><lpage>59</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12036177</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Finn</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Addressing the needs of cultural minorities in drug treatment</article-title><source>Journal of Substance Abuse Treatment</source><year>1994</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>325</fpage><lpage>337</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7966503</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0740-5472(94)90043-4</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ellis</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Support for the effectiveness of culturally competent drug and alcohol treatment, policy planning and programme development</article-title><source>Journal of Substance Use</source><year>1999</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>35</fpage><lpage>40</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.3109/14659899909052893</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rhoades</surname><given-names>HM</given-names></name><name><surname>Creson</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Elk</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmitz</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Grabowski</surname><given-names>J</given-names><